1
00:00:01,458 --> 00:00:03,916
Part Three: Lidocaine.

2
00:00:04,166 --> 00:00:08,583
If you are having trouble eating
and swallowing due to the mucositis,

3
00:00:08,583 --> 00:00:13,208
often the next step is to add a numbing
rinse to numb your mouth and throat.

4
00:00:13,208 --> 00:00:17,833
We use 2% viscous lidocaine
to rinse your mouth with.

5
00:00:17,833 --> 00:00:21,458
Use 10 to 15ml to
rinse your mouth with.

6
00:00:21,458 --> 00:00:25,083
If your areas of pain are deep
in the back of the throat

7
00:00:25,083 --> 00:00:29,666
or in the neck or esophagus,
you can also swallow the lidocaine.

8
00:00:29,916 --> 00:00:33,541
This will provide your mouth and or throat
a 15 minute

9
00:00:33,541 --> 00:00:38,250
window of numbness, during
which you can eat and drink more easily.

10
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:41,666
You can use lidocaine before every meal.

11
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:45,958
If there are small areas of pain,
you can also use a Q-Tip

12
00:00:45,958 --> 00:00:49,541
to dab lidocaine
in the specific area of mucositis

13
00:00:49,541 --> 00:00:53,833
that is causing you discomfort
or preventing you from eating.

14
00:00:53,833 --> 00:00:57,875
Please be sure that when using lidocaine
and eating that you sit

15
00:00:57,875 --> 00:01:03,083
upright and swallow food carefully
so it goes down the esophagus.

16
00:01:03,083 --> 00:01:06,833
We do not want you to aspirate
food or liquid.

17
00:01:08,583 --> 00:01:09,416
Also,

18
00:01:09,416 --> 00:01:10,083
be careful

19
00:01:10,083 --> 00:01:13,083
when chewing
since your tongue will be numb.

20
00:01:13,083 --> 00:01:15,833
You want to chew slowly and carefully

21
00:01:15,833 --> 00:01:20,166
so you do not bite your tongue
or your gums accidentally.
